cation newer than or equal to V201909 with `$vocabulary` node present', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://example.com/new-meta-with-vocab"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'JsonMetaSchema built with the given id and a vocabularies map containing all entries from the `$vocabulary` node. For example, if `$vocabulary` = {"core": true, "applicator": false}, the resulting JsonMetaSchema’s `vocabularies` map should be {"core": true, "applicator": false}.', 'description': 'The meta‑schema’s specification is V201909 or newer and the schema node contains a `$vocabulary` object. The method must initialise the builder’s vocabularies map, iterate over each property, and store the boolean values. The final JsonMetaSchema should expose the same map.'}]}, {'group': 'Null SchemaValidatorsConfig (should default to empty config)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://example.com/null-config-meta"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'JsonMetaSchema built with the given id and without any vocabularies (builder’s `vocabularies` remains null). The method must treat a null `config` as if a new `SchemaValidatorsConfig()` were supplied.', 'description': 'Pass `null` for the `SchemaValidatorsConfig`. The method should not throw NPE and should behave the same as when an empty config is supplied.'}]}, {'group': 'Null id argument (should raise IllegalArgumentException)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': 'null'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'IllegalArgumentException (or NullPointerException) is thrown because the `id` argument is required for locating the meta‑schema.', 'description': 'Verify that the method validates its `id` parameter and fails fast when it is `null`.'}]}, {'group': '$vocabulary present with non‑boolean values', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://example.com/non‑boolean‑vocab"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'JsonMetaSchema built with a vocabularies map where each entry’s value is the result of `JsonNode.booleanValue()`. Non‑boolean nodes (e.g., numbers, strings) are coerced to `false`. For a schema containing `$vocabulary:{"core":1,"applicator":"yes"}` the resulting map is {"core":false,"applicator":false}.', 'description': 'When the meta‑schema version is V201909 or newer, the method iterates over the `$vocabulary` object regardless of the actual JSON node types. This test ensures that non‑boolean values are handled gracefully (converted to `false`).'}]}, {'group': '$vocabulary present but empty object', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://example.com/empty‑vocab"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'JsonMetaSchema built with an empty vocabularies map (size\u202f0). The builder’s `vocabularies` is non‑null but contains no entries.', 'description': 'A `$vocabulary` node exists but has no properties. The method should still initialise the map (because the version check passes) and leave it empty.'}]}, {'group': '$vocabulary entries with explicit null values', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://example.com/null‑value‑vocab"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'JsonMetaSchema built with a vocabularies map where null entries are interpreted as `false`. For `$vocabulary:{"core":null}` the resulting map is {"core":false}.', 'description': 'Ensures that a `$vocabulary` property whose value is JSON `null` does not cause an exception and is treated as `false` by `booleanValue()`.'}]}, {'group': 'Specification exactly V201909 (boundary condition)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'id', 'value': '"http://example.com/boundary‑v201909"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'JsonMetaSchema built with vocabularies